late with age.**\n   - This option explains that AGEs are naturally occurring proteins that accumulate with age. While it provides information about the natural presence of AGEs, it does not directly address the link between meat consumption and asthma in children. It does not weaken the claim about meat and asthma.\n\nAfter analyzing all the options, the one that most questions the given statement is Option B. It introduces the idea that AGEs can come from sources other than meat, thereby casting doubt on the specific link between meat consumption and asthma in children.\n</think>\n<answer>\nB\n</answer>",
