 B, what is the speed of the train?\n# Question:\nWhat is the speed of the train?\n# Options:\nA) 50 mph\nB) 75 mph\nC) 100 mph\nD) 120 mph\nLet's solve this step by step.\n<|Assistant|> <think>\nTo determine the speed of the train, we can use the formula for speed, which is:\n\n\\[ \\text{Speed} = \\frac{\\text{Distance}}{\\text{Time}} \\]\n\nFrom the context provided:\n- The distance between City A and City B is 300 miles.\n- The time taken to travel this distance is 3 hours.\n\nNow, we can plug these values into the formula:\n\n\\[ \\text{Speed} = \\frac{300 \\text{ miles}}{3 \\text{ hours}} \\]\n\nLet's perform the calculation:\n\n\\[ \\text{Speed} = \\frac{300}{3} = 100 \\text{ mph} \\]\n\nTherefore, the speed of the train is 100 mph.\n\nThe correct answer is:\n<answer>\nC\n</answer>\n</think>",
