s.\n\n### Ranking Analysis:\n\nGiven the conditions, let's rank the subjects:\n\n- From Condition 3, \\( M1 > P + E \\).\n- From Condition 1, \\( P + M1 = E + M2 \\), which implies \\( M1 \\) is significantly higher than \\( P \\) and \\( E \\).\n- From Condition 2, \\( P + M2 > E + M1 \\), which implies \\( M2 \\) is higher than \\( M1 \\) but not as high as \\( M1 \\).\n\nThus, the ranking from highest to lowest should be:\n1. Major one (\\( M1 \\))\n2. Major two (\\( M2 \\))\n3. Political (\\( P \\))\n4. English (\\( E \\))\n\nTherefore, the correct ranking is:\nC) Major subject one, major subject two, politics, english.\n</think>\n<answer>C</answer>",
