urveyed.\n   - To find the number of students who preferred strawberry, we calculate \\( 30\\% \\) of 120.\n   - Convert the percentage to a decimal: \\( 30\\% = 0.30 \\).\n   - Multiply the total number of students by this decimal: \\( 120 \\times 0.30 \\).\n\n3. **Perform the multiplication:**\n   \\[\n   120 \\times 0.30 = 36\n   \\]\n\nThus, the number of students who preferred strawberry is 36.\n\n</think>\n<answer>\n36\n</answer>",
