o fewer new and potentially more effective drugs being developed. Consequently, the overall quality of drugs available to consumers might decrease, which would not benefit consumers. Therefore, the presence of me-too drugs can indirectly benefit consumers by maintaining the incentive for companies to develop innovative drugs, which could lead to new and potentially better drugs.\n\nConsidering the editorial's argument that me-too drugs can lead to price reductions, the option that most strengthens this argument is the one that supports the idea that me-too drugs can maintain the incentive for companies to develop innovative drugs, thereby benefiting consumers indirectly through the availability of new and potentially better drugs.\n\nThus, the correct option is D.\n</think>\n<answer>\nD\n</answer>",
