, it makes a generalization about Comrade Bethune based on his behavior compared to others.\n   - **Option D**: \"Silver and copper are both metals with electrical conductivity, but the resistivity of silver is lower, so silver is more suitable to be a conductive material than copper.\"\n     - This statement fits the form of an analogical argument. It compares two specific objects (silver and copper) with attributes (electrical conductivity) and then infers a similarity in another attribute (suitability as a conductive material) based on a different attribute (resistivity).\n\n3. **Conclusion**: Based on the analysis, Option D is the only one that fits the definition of an analogical argument.\n</think>\n<answer>\nD\n</answer>",
