e argument. The argument does not claim that understanding sentences is impossible if they are uninterrupted streams of sound; it only states that this is how non-native speakers perceive them.\n   - **Option D**: \"People pay less close attention to the way their own language sounds than they do to the way an unfamiliar language sounds.\"\n     - This option is not directly relevant to the argument. The argument does not discuss the level of attention people pay to their own language versus unfamiliar languages.\n\n5. **Conclusion**:\n   - The assumption that supports the argument is that native speakers' perception of sentences as separate words is not more accurate than that of non-native speakers.\n   - Therefore, the correct answer is Option A.\n</think>\n<answer>\nA\n</answer>",
