qual treatment in inheritance, which is a form of equal protection from the state. It aligns with the context of equal rights and protection, so it does not violate the right to equality.\n   \n4. **Conclusion:**\n   - Based on the analysis, the option that represents a violation of the right to equality is Option C, as it involves a refusal to provide equal access to education based on a characteristic (physical disability) that is not relevant to the ability to receive education.\n</think>\n<answer>C</answer>",
