lem, let's analyze the given data step by step and compare the percentages of students preferring each ice cream flavor in both schools.\n\n### Context and Data:\n- **Overall Survey Results:**\n  - Chocolate: 40%\n  - Vanilla: 30%\n  - Strawberry: 30%\n\n- **School A Results:**\n  - Chocolate: 50%\n  - Vanilla: 30%\n  - Strawberry: 20%\n\n- **School B Results:**\n  - Chocolate: 30%\n  - Vanilla: 40%\n  - Strawberry: 30%\n\n### Question:\nWe need to determine which of the given statements is true based on the survey results.\n\n### Analysis of Each Statement:\n\n**A) School A has a higher percentage of students preferring chocolate than School B.**\n- School A: 50%\n- School B: 30%\n- **Conclusion:** This statement is true because 50% (School A) is indeed higher than 30% (School B).\n\n**B) School B has a higher percentage of students preferring vanilla than School A.**\n- School A: 30%\n- School B: 40%\n- **Conclusion:** This statement is false because 40% (School B) is not higher than 30% (School A).\n\n**C) School A has a higher percentage of students preferring strawberry than School B.**\n- School A: 20%\n- School B: 30%\n- **Conclusion:** This statement is false because 20% (School A) is not higher than 30% (School B).\n\n**D) School B has a higher percentage of students preferring chocolate than School A.**\n- School A: 50%\n- School B: 30%\n- **Conclusion:** This statement is false because 30% (School B) is not higher than 50% (School A).\n\n### Final Answer:\nBased on the analysis, the correct statement is:\n</think>\n<answer>A</answer>",
