ny given information.\n\nD) **A doesn't business, b doesn't business**\n   - This option states that A is not on a business trip and B is not on a business trip. This is consistent with Statement 1 (\\( A \\lor B \\lor C \\)) because C is on a business trip.\n\nGiven the analysis, both options C and D are consistent with the given information. However, the problem asks for the option that can be derived, implying a single definitive answer. \n\nSince option C directly follows from the given statements without any contradictions, it is the most straightforward and correct option.\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is C.\n</think>\n<answer>C</answer>",
